pra: 0166 - wedge-proof logging: strat flushes the ring itself on chunk failure

DRAFT (not committed; produced by the eMMC speed-work agent, lives in
research/driver-specs/emmc-work/). Generated against the reconstructed
CI-built tree: pristine xnu-8796.141.3 + stack 0001..0165 with pre-skips
0031/0041/0097/0099/0127/0129, GNU patch -p1 --fuzz=0 (index lines
stripped). Verify with GNU `patch -p1 --fuzz=0 --dry-run`, NOT git apply
(git 2.56 skip-detects already-applied hunks with rc=0).

PROBLEM: every multi-block wedge so far destroyed its own evidence. The
pralog flusher writes through the same strat path and shares pra_emmc_lock
with strat, so a wedged card leaves ring N byte-identical to ring N-1
(ring20/ring21) - the wedge forensics (which phase failed, which status
word, did the lines ever clear) were lost three boots in a row.

CHANGES:

1. pra_log_panic_flush's core loop + header write refactored into
   pra_log_flush_locked(start, blocks, total, seq), called with
   pra_emmc_lock HELD. New pra_log_strat_flush(force) writes the newest
   128 ring blocks (64 KiB tail) + header from strat's chunk-failure path
   (strat already holds the lock) and again, force=true, when the 2-strike
   latch fires. Bounded: on a healthy card ~0.2 s of writes; on a wedged
   card the first write_raw fails EBUSY after its bounded ready-poll and
   the attempt is one printed line. Rate-limited to one per 10 s with the
   suppressed count carried on the next line; the latch flush bypasses the
   limit (at most once per boot, terminal event).
2. The periodic flusher's pra_log_write_sector switches lck_mtx_lock ->
   lck_mtx_try_lock and returns EBUSY when strat owns the line: it skips
   that sector this tick instead of queueing behind a strat request for
   minutes. The existing EBUSY retry logic absorbs the new return path.
3. Every CMD18 event prints with its forensics: the chunk-failure line
   gains the chunk's last status word (pra_emmc_multi_last_status, set at
   every read_multi exit; EBUSY exits carry the PRESENT_STATE CMD/DAT
   inhibit bits instead); pra_emmc_recover() now reports whether the lines
   actually released ("recover: CMD12+reset, CMD/DAT lines released /
   STILL BUSY", rate-limited 1/10 s with a running recover count). Ladder
   transitions already print (0164).
4. pra_emmc_read_sector's busy exit now uses pra_emmc_busy_note() - the
   0164-sized gap WORKLOG section 11 called out: the DEFAULT path was the
   only one still printing card-busy at line rate. A healthy boot prints
   nothing either way; a wedge boot now rate-limits like the multi path.
5. pra_log_thread's header seq promoted to a file-scope pra_log_seq so the
   strat flush writes headers in the same sequence space.

DEFAULT BOOT: byte-identical behaviour unless the card misbehaves - every
changed line is on a failure or busy path; the flusher try_lock only
differs from lock when strat holds the lock, which the old code would have
blocked on.

STACKING: on top of 0164+0165. 0004/0005/0006 build on this patch.

